   "source": [
    "# Time-Series Regression Model: Housing Price Volatility\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook estimates whether **policy uncertainty** (from Fed meeting minutes) helps predict **housing price volatility** (from CAAR market reports).\n",
    "\n",
    "We fit an **Autoregressive OLS model** of the form:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{Vol}_t = \\alpha + \\beta_1 \\cdot \\text{UncertaintyScore}_t + \\beta_2 \\cdot \\text{Vol}_{t-1} + \\varepsilon_t$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $\\text{Vol}_t$ = housing price volatility at time $t$\n",
    "- $\\text{UncertaintyScore}_t$ = linguistic uncertainty score from meeting minutes\n",
    "- $\\text{Vol}_{t-1}$ = last month's volatility (the autoregressive lag term)\n",
    "- $\\varepsilon_t$ = error term\n",
    "\n",
    "**Your job:** Fill in every `# TODO` block and answer the reflection questions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning goals:**\n",
    "- Understand how to structure time-series data for regression\n",
    "- Learn what a lagged variable is and why it matters\n",
    "- Interpret OLS regression output (coefficients, p-values, R²)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "575d3210-1551-4e10-b9a1-ff8e9975658d",
